#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259731 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18243450-8bc5-5ba5-92ae-2a12b967b1f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462145} {:answer/id #uuid "53526394-7618-5253-b8b8-39da508afb42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462146}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186462145} :answer-field/id #uuid "701895d0-d3f5-5fd1-99cc-2ef0e7db9adb" :answer-field/key "${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462826} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb1353f6-b0c0-5194-a209-45cfa89e9762" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462147} {:answer/id #uuid "67103826-f812-5a9c-a5d1-e93ca05c2123" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462148}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186462148} :answer-field/id #uuid "c24c9f12-a9c4-502d-a521-d96ff0a52d43" :answer-field/key "${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x\\ge 1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462827} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "973fe3d8-28f4-5ce5-afa3-e107736244b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462149} {:answer/id #uuid "2f92d4a6-c6ba-5890-bc7a-b9c3b83bf58f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462150}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186462149} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b065414-05f8-5b5f-b809-0e2f2975f5ea" :answer-field/key "${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,xy\\ne 0}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462828}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "bd4c2e21-ea3a-5149-9740-8c2a599beff2" :question/math-academy-id "q-124782" :question/problem "Which of the following regions are simply connected?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/7d/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/c3/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nLet's now examine our regions in turn.\n\n- Region ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 4}$ is *not* simply connected. The region contains all the points of ${R}^{2}$ except those on the ellipse ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4.$ Thus, the region is formed by two disjoint pieces and, therefore, is not even a connected region.\n\n- Region ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x\\ge 1}$  is simply connected. It's a plane region without holes.\n\n- Region ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,xy\\ne 0}$ is *not* simply connected.  The region contains all the points of ${R}^{2}$ except those on the coordinate axes.  Thus, the region is formed by four disjoint pieces and, therefore, is not even a connected region.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x\\ge 1}$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259804 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e410ddf-84e2-5349-b99f-7b10cce11cec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}2z\\,\\text{d}x+3x\\,\\text{d}y-4y\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257608} {:answer/id #uuid "8e11896f-16e5-5f59-bbed-02cfb68e20a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}3x\\,\\text{d}x-4y\\,\\text{d}y+2z\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258034} {:answer/id #uuid "9648d6f8-5662-55bf-8371-9e2f6c4805c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}-4y\\,\\text{d}x+2z\\,\\text{d}y+3x\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258105} {:answer/id #uuid "be39d050-270c-5115-8d0f-7cd3ce274da8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}2\\,\\text{d}x+3\\,\\text{d}y-4\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258443} {:answer/id #uuid "e622dbb6-dbf6-50da-90af-70479db8a9bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}(2z+3x-4y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258777}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186257608} :answer-field/id #uuid "72c0c87b-9ed0-5e85-a70e-4bc5daad194c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259228}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "78e032bd-88b9-59d8-89ba-60a2eb488ce7" :question/math-academy-id "q-125413" :question/problem "Let $F(x,y,z)=2z\\,i+3x\\,j-4y\\,k$ and let $C$ be a path in ${R}^{3}.$ Which of the following is equivalent to $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given a piecewise-smooth path $C$ and a vector field \n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=P(x,y,z)\\,i+Q(x,y,z)\\,j+R(x,y,z)\\,k\n$$\n\ndefined on $C,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{C}P(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y+R(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{C}2z\\,\\text{d}x+3x\\,\\text{d}y-4y\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259805 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19e81440-e84d-56cd-bb58-ec161c442251" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}x\\,\\text{d}x+({y}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257003} {:answer/id #uuid "5f494e8c-ad73-595a-bf25-8c0366227915" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}({x}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x+y\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257618} {:answer/id #uuid "7b07b399-bcf2-5d7e-8ea4-1477d0096940" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}({y}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x+x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257873} {:answer/id #uuid "8f63ee0f-d6d5-55d0-a96d-faabbd6baae3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}(x-3y)\\,\\text{d}x+2\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258042} {:answer/id #uuid "fba49b65-428e-5726-bf94-6db8e1ed2b78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}2\\,\\text{d}x+(x-3y)\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258982}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186258042} :answer-field/id #uuid "021dcd34-65cf-5872-b83c-9f85620594f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259035}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ab23b1e6-350e-57c6-bc34-78c226b2bb0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-125416" :question/problem "Let $F(x,y)=(x-3y)\\,i+2\\,j$ and let $C$ be the path defined by $r(t)=⟨t,\\,{t}^{2}+1⟩$ for $t\\in [0,1].$ Which of the following is equivalent to $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given a piecewise-smooth path $C$ and a vector field \n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j\n$$\n\ndefined on $C,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{C}P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{C}(x-3y)\\,\\text{d}x+2\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259806 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5eb6d40c-1738-5868-a121-ed6bf6c0d399" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}(2y-3x)\\,\\text{d}x-4\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257614} {:answer/id #uuid "751bbc81-29f2-5e3a-8e2b-798df9ec806c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}x\\,\\text{d}x+(3y-1)\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257809} {:answer/id #uuid "88ae962d-8869-54c0-82fc-70c5851fef4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}(3x-1)\\,\\text{d}x+y\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257980} {:answer/id #uuid "bcb0d958-9542-52b7-aab9-12ab08f18e7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}(3y-1)\\,\\text{d}x+x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258428} {:answer/id #uuid "e7c032c0-a028-5aad-8373-05466f052f8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}4\\,\\text{d}x-(2y-3x)\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258789}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186258789} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f8a6dd0-aae9-5825-810c-1c9c92473b84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259146}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0bb48414-d307-548b-9146-c35b5549d965" :question/math-academy-id "q-125417" :question/problem "Let $F(x,y)=4\\,i-(2y-3x)\\,j$ and let $C$ be the path defined by $r(t)=⟨t,\\,3t-1⟩$ for $t\\in [0,1].$ Which of the following is equivalent to $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given a piecewise-smooth path $C$ and a vector field \n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j\n$$\n\ndefined on $C,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{C}P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{C}4\\,\\text{d}x-(2y-3x)\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259807 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6801901d-9ee9-5371-8b4b-d5db2b6a1458" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}\\,i-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}\\,j+{z}^{2}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257701} {:answer/id #uuid "769ce3bb-7d2e-5ce5-b0b0-28c4cea5482a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "∇({x}^{2}-y+2z)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257826} {:answer/id #uuid "93d7b961-74bb-5506-ae9a-49293428f19f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}∇({x}^{2}-y+2z)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258084} {:answer/id #uuid "9e78f156-7020-55eb-a260-6ad7cfa75ccf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{2}\\,i-y\\,j+2z\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258176} {:answer/id #uuid "dc333661-b4ae-5e54-bf73-e30af54e6c08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x\\,i-j+2\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258700}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186258176} :answer-field/id #uuid "25124abe-208b-52ab-a6ab-e1f14753fd21" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259098}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "a8a91190-7516-5928-b654-d4cd2239861a" :question/math-academy-id "q-125423" :question/problem "If $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-y\\,\\text{d}y+2z\\,\\text{d}z\n$$ is equivalent to $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$ for some piecewise smooth curve $C,$ then $F(x,y,z)=$" :question/worked-solution "Given a piecewise-smooth path $C$ and a vector field \n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=P(x,y,z)\\,i+Q(x,y,z)\\,j+R(x,y,z)\\,k\n$$\n\ndefined on $C,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y+R\\,\\text{d}z\n$$\n\nIn our case, $P={x}^{2},Q=-y,R=2z.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}({x}^{2}\\,i-y\\,j+2z\\,k)\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{C}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-y\\,\\text{d}y+2z\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $F={x}^{2}\\,i-y\\,j+2z\\,k.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259813 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a312728-759b-5a18-bc9a-7a468e2c468e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462181} {:answer/id #uuid "b006ccd8-dbf9-52a5-8de6-8656396b4437" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462182}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186462181} :answer-field/id #uuid "c09c4b26-8176-500e-9d72-7fa8141a088c" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462844} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "822889f3-1878-5472-943f-bc21421aa019" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462183} {:answer/id #uuid "3f2cd909-af16-5666-9ee5-08e066d042c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462184}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186462184} :answer-field/id #uuid "e45bb2d9-7504-598f-8971-17193667fabf" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462845} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c27fd31-ee21-5aab-a03c-e98f38a45ae9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462185} {:answer/id #uuid "e661237d-bcf6-5e01-b2dc-8992ab58d984" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462186}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186462186} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebc3f15f-2730-55a5-bdbe-6cc6317a24d4" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462846}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0a58b62d-04d0-5a47-b1b2-408fc180c352" :question/math-academy-id "q-125487" :question/problem "![](images/9d/9da7dc42ad4e9eb5b6df7c42f06d7a0f7767820693f8e99e073c7b8bd7e93441.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above, and let $C$ be the path along the segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.\n$$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0\n$$ is false, while statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0\n$$ is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$  works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](images/14/14e94a2c5d0faabff1beeadeccb6999aa2edd71fce06fff8a2655db74e585eba.png)\n\nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.\n$$\n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0\n$$ is true. It's clear from the picture below that if we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](images/c5/c54487081f2150216b7e41b1351f0f7b19c794b140297789f19d9afe830bd7b1.png)\n\nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0;\n$$ $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0\n$$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259814 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d53d1d6-b5c4-5b67-bf25-7d27d099f803" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462187} {:answer/id #uuid "7ea8a4ee-7a15-5906-a035-85b03d8a5bf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462188}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186462187} :answer-field/id #uuid "c81ca5e2-2c88-5480-af0e-02088df15e01" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462847} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f4889ea-7df9-5050-8467-49e0a39fea58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462189} {:answer/id #uuid "77388560-2b05-5177-b365-d77d025c0040" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462190}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186462190} :answer-field/id #uuid "e54e19c2-5a75-508b-8a0e-b667cad3e56c" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462848} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21087b76-e92c-5bb7-b96b-7c74da65d9f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462191} {:answer/id #uuid "0c4cb97b-af71-57cc-ae8c-5ba9597eb620" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462192}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186462192} :answer-field/id #uuid "432876d0-b578-5b13-9052-5619b6ddf8f1" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462849}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "35e675be-a5b1-5d4c-9024-2339a508b912" :question/math-academy-id "q-125491" :question/problem "![](images/f0/f0daaf51b1aab267c11b8457b0e7e1480ff5aabd3acaa15a07f54625c6d8103d.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above, and let $C$ be the path where the curve is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.\n$$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0\n$$ is false, while statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0\n$$ is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$  works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](images/17/1764bfc51a25475162a70bad7239a36f5d099aa6157c71ed7ed3e02e474eb906.png)\n\n \n\nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.\n$$\n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0\n$$ is true. It's clear from the picture below that if we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](images/05/059731f0cac61f19382172192c6a9f7f366ecb758767797f9bc8311faa3865af.png)\n\n \n\nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0;\n$$ $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0\n$$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259815 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "534628ec-e086-5d85-8e31-fc04c99a5f8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462193} {:answer/id #uuid "aa45667f-b444-5719-9295-4e64b477febd" :answe