ticle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.\n$$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0\n$$ is true, while statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0\n$$ is false. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](images/c0/c075bf6fa60af07e70569395b257d25bb53f5edab8ff14f4a772271c9df7e153.png)\n\n \nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.\n$$\n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0\n$$ is false. It's clear from the picture below that if we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](images/41/41528079b285fb3ba20fcac0bd28f42ed7981a775938286654cf7319c1e8a6c6.png)\n\n \nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0\n$$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259817 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25c37202-f845-5fe8-8a7a-1db1f298b82f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463464} {:answer/id #uuid "814c544b-ea3b-5e5e-85a8-e01671b5faa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463465}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463464} :answer-field/id #uuid "72d39b77-fe29-5793-a0fb-0f2c0ded2a24" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464666} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66c009aa-e253-537e-b9ea-d64ce314b9a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463466} {:answer/id #uuid "ee7535b0-5862-5dfa-963f-9d8f8799fc40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463467}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463467} :answer-field/id #uuid "401ef778-f261-5f37-b35b-442681079175" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464667} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe4ca179-59d3-5f0e-a769-a1d46a8dd48d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463468} {:answer/id #uuid "2ae8df09-8879-50b4-8407-98178c0cb9e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463469}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463468} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecf5381b-d126-5634-9a8c-5944ea06f42d" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464668}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0ce534ad-d76e-5678-87a2-87c2bbfd4370" :question/math-academy-id "q-125500" :question/problem "![](images/8d/8dc3102ab0055d4e7dde7c79873a2c3d825fa9c803ea1ee2376a7dbe920c5535.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)$ shown above, and let $C$ be the path where the quarter circle is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.\n$$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion  of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0\n$$ is false, while statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ is true. Since the force $F$ acts perpendicular to the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B,$ it neither helps nor hinders its motion. \n\n![](images/ac/ac9d8388e73a33df98ac7f04fe161ae75b27b4b01a79213c07e10d43c328d747.png)\n\nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0\n$$ is false. If we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then the situation with regards to the work done by $F$ is similar to the previous case.\n\n![](images/92/92e6f3ca98d7adbb34765307c0c570f55ce85f7f10cf6bef28bdb93d68a0c1cb.png)\n\n \nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259818 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cfa6683-6722-5eeb-96a9-3db5e8cf9923" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463470} {:answer/id #uuid "75906f44-44f3-5c13-92f4-cc5703a4776e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463471}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463470} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8d2d0d3-81db-50eb-a9fb-a003de2f2449" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464669} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4736c250-e772-5723-98dc-f93776c74c93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463472} {:answer/id #uuid "fca386ca-2828-5d6c-9232-724a2e7d32ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463473}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463473} :answer-field/id #uuid "63e272b7-517f-5dd8-b86c-d72d0456faf3" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464670} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6a6e849-4c6b-52a5-b5eb-bf0993666973" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463474} {:answer/id #uuid "7c6c0bcb-c01b-55d2-88c8-5dd7ed78b8a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463475}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463474} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec32f74a-0dc2-5daf-8e33-34c8db66e97a" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464671}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "eb3b3139-68a2-57de-b20c-f84dd8321120" :question/math-academy-id "q-125501" :question/problem "![](images/ee/ee674d6140d9326894d607ca9a3feede580ce68bd56ca762a013a9602a657832.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)$ shown above, and let $C$ be the path where the curve is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.\n$$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion  of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0\n$$ is false, while statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ is true. Since the force $F$ acts perpendicular to the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B,$ it neither helps nor hinders its motion. \n\n![](images/d6/d69e4c3dee5a346baae0accffc4d234b5b84e0402d107b5d1a24160a796992dd.png)\n\n \nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0\n$$ is false. If we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then the situation with regards to the work done by $F$ is similar to the previous case.\n\n![](images/61/61a1ebee96c7082485b318d5bcc1f55a42c0f4589b0aad9edf09e4deb82a2403.png)\n\n \nSo, $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0\n$$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259819 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b904a0b-0910-5626-8d87-2d88fb8897f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463476} {:answer/id #uuid "ca7170fa-1276-577a-8d37-143e3bc54016" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463477}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463476} :answer-field/id #uuid "813913cc-5007-5f69-a965-673ce565c158" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464672} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07e328df-cc3b-5f1a-a1c7-d827c0da6c08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463478} {:answer/id #uuid "4873fd1a-fd38-5b50-92b1-eb49a4809f49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463479}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463479} :answer-field/id #uuid "102